        "date": "2026-11-19T02:00:18Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(multiaxis): Rotary Parallel leaves the end face of a held end\n\nRotary Parallel ran its raster over the whole model and did not know the\nstock. On a bar held in a chuck, the pass down the chuck-side end face was\na slot one tool wide from the skin to the axis: it parted the bar.\n\nThe kind now reads the setup stock. Where the stock goes on past an end of\nthe model by more than one tool diameter, the centre of the ball does not\ngo past that end plane: the end face is left, the turned surface is\nfinished to its end, and a note names the end. A sloped entry does not\nstart past a held end. A free end, and a facing allowance of one tool\ndiameter or less, are cut as before.\n\nThe #1904 example project and program are generated again, and the guide\npages and pictures follow the new program.\n\nFixes #2343\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
